-- --opens specification (seg/WRITING.md, rule 6) for MarkDirect
-- (doc/delooping-direct.pdf, Section 3: statement M for every pointed 2-connected
-- 4-type, without a presentation): one entry per declaration, generated from
-- --opened (28 Oct 2026) and read against the note.  Kinds of openings:
--   types and levels: PtMap, PtSec, Maps.PMO, Over.Unloop, isContr, isEquiv,
--     Equiv, isSet, Hom, H4, HC, STr.Same, Lifting.Ex / Un / qs (the hypotheses
--     (E), (U) and q_*), Triples (on the declarations after a triple), the
--     fibre types Fib / fpt / Triple.F / f0, Deloopable / fibO (the declaration
--     after dl), SC4 / PtProp.PP / P4 (uA: K(A,3) as an element of SC4),
--     O2 / O3 (s3-paths at K(B,4)), Trunc.carrier / image;
--   the carrier HC opened to Quot.Q and its image (comp-zero-r, ck, c, rF):
--     extra (ii) of doc/pi3-s2-postnikov.pdf, as in mapfib.opens;
--   index arithmetic: two, three, four, five, NatArith.plus (Lemma 1 at
--     (S3, K(B,4)); uA, rA: K(A,3) with three against Lev's K (suc two));
--   by-definition steps of the text: G, h, t, dl (local definitions; t and
--     its equation t-eq are stated before t is locked); Psi.psi (cls, as
--     MapBR.ExBR.cls); Zab (h.1 at hcomp, cls); RStar (the statement "r^*
--     bijective into Z"); Mark.Marked, Acs.Y / y, uA (M at K(A,3) is
--     SourceS3.Final.right); MarkLoop.LMark.At.LMarked / rs (LMarked is
--     RStar at Omega Y); Equivalences.compose (rF: the composite q_R then r^*);
--     hcl (classes are the inc of STr);
--   extras, not steps of the text: the aliases KZ2 / kz2 against
--     KK[Z].K two of FibP (G, PS, chain, null), as in mapfib.opens.
-- t is locked after t-eq (dl opened the construction of realise-equiv
-- through t before).
-- Check: segd All.seg --opens markdirect.opens ; every line "nothing else opened".
